# Broadleaf tree after Pałubicki et al. (2009). Buds grow toward free space
# in a crown envelope (space colonization, Runions et al. 2007); the light
# the buds catch flows to the base and back out to them (Borchert-Honda
# vigour); a bud grows as many internodes in a year as its vigour allows.
# Apical control is strong in a young tree and relaxes with age, which
# raises a trunk and then spreads the crown. A lateral bud without the
# vigour for a long shoot still leafs out each year as a short shoot while
# it has light. Shaded buds die, and a branch with no living bud is shed,
# which clears the lower stem.
#
# A stem may lean, wander a little at every internode, and divide low into
# several equal stems, as open-grown maples and oaks do; dividing at the
# ground makes a many-stemmed shrub.
#
# Buds and leaves are opposite and decussate, as in maples, or alternate on
# a spiral, as in oaks and cherries (leaves_per_node, divergence). Leaves
# fall every year or, on evergreens, stay leaf_years. Once old enough,
# short shoots in the light carry flowers or fruit at their tips (blooms):
# blossoms, berry clusters or hanging catkins, whichever look the species
# gives them.
#
# Revision 4 (plant forms F5): a thorny species (thorns 1) carries a thorn
# beside each bud, thorn_length long at thorn_angle to its shoot. A tree
# with a `life` dies at that age: its buds die and its leaves fall, and its
# dead branches drop one by one, each with the chance snag_fall a year, so
# it stands as a snag.
#
# Revision 5 (plant forms F7): in a steady wind (wind above 0, blowing
# toward +X) shoots bend downwind under a tropism toward (wind, -1, 0)
# of elasticity droop + wind_bend * wind, and a shoot tip heading upwind
# (its heading's X below -wind_kill) dies, so the crown grows as a flag
# on its lee side.
#
# Revision 6 (phyllotaxis P1): leaves_per_node buds and leaves stand at a
# node (2, a pair, or 1), each node turned divergence degrees from the one
# below: the names every leaf-bearing program shares, which the rules at
# the vascular plants set from a taxon's leaf_arrangement and
# phyllotaxis_pattern. They replace alternate (0 is leaves_per_node 2, 1 is
# 1), with the same defaults: a pair crossing the pair below, or a single
# bud on the golden-angle spiral. More than two at a node draw as a pair.
#
# Revision 7 (spec rework M7): a thorn is a spine, not a leaf.
#
# Revision 8 (spec rework P6): the first year the plant is adult, from
# which it flowers, is adult_age, the name the programs that measure it
# by the plant's age share, which the rule at the seed plants sets from
# a taxon's juvenile_period_years. It replaces bloom_age, with the same
# default.
#
# Revision 9 (crown calibration): short shoots live while they have
# light, for up to bud_years (default 40, was 12), so a crown keeps
# leafing inside until its own shade, not its age, ends its short shoots:
# an open-grown crown holds the leaf area per crown area of the USDA
# Urban Tree Database's open-grown trees, and its inner leaves grow in
# shade. A short shoot's yearly leaves carry their own turn
# (`leaf(size, roll, pitch, level)`), one module each where
# `[ &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(size) ]` with a roll left behind takes five, as
# the maples' have since growth plan G1, so a crown that keeps its short
# shoots stays within the module limit.
#
# Revision 10 (crown form, step A): a year's shoot is a growth unit of
# unit_nodes nodes for each internode its vigour allows, each internode /
# unit_nodes long, with a bud and a leaf at every node, as real shoots
# carry many nodes on short internodes. Only some of its buds may grow
# long shoots: the last long_share of its nodes (acrotony, as in oaks,
# whose buds cluster at the twig tip) or, with bud_base 1, the first
# (basitony, as in shrubs that renew from the base). Those buds grow out
# where they have the vigour and leaf out as short shoots where they do
# not, as before; on the short_share of its nodes next to those, buds
# grow short shoots (K), which leaf out in the light but never grow out;
# the rest stay latent, as a growth unit's buds grade from long shoots to
# short ones to latent. So branches come in clusters at a year's shoot's
# tip with leaves along the wood between them, not one long branch every
# internode.
#
# What the maples did on top of broadleaf is now broadleaf's, off unless a
# lineage turns it on, so every broadleaf limb can live by its own light:
# shedding of limbs whose tips collect too little light for the wood they
# carry (shed_ratio; Pałubicki et al. 2009), dormant buds at each node
# that sprout where light reaches (dormant_buds, delayed reiteration),
# space that returns where limbs are shed (space_renew), forks after a
# shoot ends in flowers (terminal_bloom) and tips with no free space that
# abort (apex_death). The space tool is space@2 with broadleaf's
# ellipsoid. The rules at the seed plants set these from a lineage's
# characters (bud_position, shoot_leaves, epicormic, self_pruning,
# flowering_position).
#
# Revision 11 (crown form, step B): the crown grows its own outline
# inside a loose region. The free space of space@2 fills a region
# room_width times the crown's radius and room_height times its height,
# so it keeps the crown's inside full without drawing its edge. A shoot's
# nodes are shorter by 1 / (1 + (wood / path_half)²), its wood measured
# from the base, as water has farther to climb, where a limb's wood
# (`limb`: branches off an axis that goes on past them) counts limb_path
# times; so the tree's height and its limbs' reach level off by
# themselves, and limb_path sets how wide the crown spreads against how
# tall it grows. A tip's light gathers as a leaf's photosynthesis does,
# half of full light's at light_half (vigour@1 saturation), so shaded
# shoots inside a stand keep growing. The stem holds itself upright
# (leader_rate) and limbs hold their set_point angle from straight up
# (incline_rate), and the wood bends under its own weight and its leaves'
# (bend@1, from wood_density and wood_modulus), keeping bend_set of each
# year's sag; the stem and a fork's stems, held by reaction wood, take
# stem_bend of theirs. A tip with no free space left leafs out as a short
# shoot does.
#
# Revision 12 (growth plan G2.3a): a starting base with no values. Each
# parameter given as a number is `param name;`, and the lineage programs
# that extend it (`acanthaceae`, `apiales`, `asterales`, `betulaceae`,
# `bignoniaceae`, `caprifoliaceae`, `cornaceae`, `ericaceae`, `fabales`,
# `fagaceae`, `grossulariaceae`, `malvaceae`, `moraceae`, `nothofagaceae`,
# `oleaceae`, `ranunculales`, `rhamnaceae`, `rhizophoraceae`, `rosaceae`,
# `salicaceae`, `simmondsiaceae`, `viburnaceae`, `zygophyllaceae`,
# `sapindaceae`) give the values their species leave unset, as this
# program's defaults were until then.
#
# Revision 13 (leaf life): leaves and blooms live as long as their
# parameters say, no longer one year more. What a step makes is born at
# the step's end, so a rule that ends a part by its age counts the step it
# is in (`age + dt >=`).
#
# Revision 14 (dioecy): in a dioecious species (dioecious 1, from the
# sexual system its taxa state) a plant whose own draw `sex` is below a
# half is male: its blooms are `bloom_male`, drawn as its blooms are in
# bud and flower and fallen where they would set fruit. The rest are
# female and bloom and fruit as before; so does a plant that bears both
# sexes (dioecious 0). bloom_male is declared last, so the other organs
# keep their places.
#
# Revision 15 (crown form, item 1): the region narrows among neighbours
# (space@4). In the open it is the same ellipsoid as before; among
# neighbours, or at a stand's edge, each height and side of it is scaled
# as far as the front a crown as wide for its depth grows (Duchemin et al.
# 2018; the lineage's gravitropism that gives that width in the open, and
# its phototropism crown_phototropism) falls short under their shade. Less
# light comes from the side there, more so on a stand's side, so the crown
# grows narrower, and toward open sky at an edge.
#
# Revision 16 (woody forms: scaffold limbs and silhouettes): limbs rise
# from the stem and arch outward as they lengthen, as open-grown oaks'
# do: a shoot on a limb holds a set point limb_arch degrees farther from
# upright for each metre of limb wood below it, up to limb_set_max, so
# the crown rounds into a dome where it drew a cone. Near the crown's top
# (above flat_top of its height) every shoot, the stem's too, levels out,
# as all the axes of an umbrella thorn do (Troll's model), and the crown
# spreads into a flat top. With bole_clear, a branch whose base stands
# below the crown's base as it rises is shed, so the tree stands on a
# clear trunk; never at or above where the stem forks. The region's
# profile, an ellipse widest at its middle until now, is widest at
# crown_widest of its depth and fills toward a cylinder with
# crown_fullness. All are off, or as before, unless a lineage or species
# sets them, so every crown grows as it did.
#
# Revision 17 (nightshades round 2): a bloom may hang on a stalk of its
# own, bloom_stalk long, as a fuchsia's flowers hang on their long
# peduncles. Off (0) unless a lineage or species sets it, so every plant
# grows as it did.
#
# Revision 18 (nightshades round 3): leaves in whorls of three or more
# (leaves_per_node 3 and up) are drawn round the node, not in pairs, and
# a bloom's stalk is shed with its bloom. Every plant whose leaves are
# alternate or opposite grows as it did.
#
# One step is one year. Angles are degrees; lengths are metres.

lsystem broadleaf 17;

# Crown envelope at maturity; it approaches this size at crown_rate per year.
param crown_height;
param crown_radius;
param crown_base;
param crown_rate;

param internode;              # length of one internode
param max_shoot;              # most internodes a bud grows in one year
param bud_break;              # vigour a lateral bud needs to grow a long shoot
param branch_angle;           # angle between a shoot and its lateral buds
param apical_young;           # Borchert-Honda lambda in a sapling
param apical;                 # and in a mature tree: near 0.5 spreads the crown
param apical_years;           # years over which apical control relaxes
param flux;                   # Borchert-Honda alpha: vigour per unit of light
param light_half;             # light at which a tip gathers half of full light's vigour; 0: in proportion
param bud_years;              # years a lateral bud lives as a short shoot while it has light
param spur_light;             # light a short shoot needs to leaf out
param shade_death;            # light below which a bud dies
param steer_weight;           # how far a shoot turns toward free space
param leaf_size;              # leaf card length including the petiole
param spur_leaf;              # leaves on short shoots are smaller
param spur_pairs;             # pairs of leaves a short shoot unfolds each year
param leaf_area;              # leaf area of a leaf card 1 m long, m²
param leaf_angle;
param leaves_per_node;        # buds and leaves at a node: 2 opposite, 1 alternate
param divergence = leaves_per_node == 2 ? 90 : 137.5;   # roll from one node to the next
param leaf_years;             # years a leaf stays on: more than 1 for evergreens
param blooms;                 # blooms at the tip of a short shoot in the light
param adult_age;              # the first year the plant is adult and flowers
param bloom_size;             # bloom card length
param bloom_angle;            # angle of a bloom to its shoot; past 90 it hangs
param bloom_area;             # leaf area of a bloom card 1 m long, m²
param dioecious;              # 1: each plant is male or female; 0: every plant bears both
param sex;                    # this plant's own draw, 0 to 1: below a half, a dioecious plant is male
param droop;
param lean;                   # the most the stem leans from upright
param wiggle;                 # spread of the random turn at each internode
param fork_height;            # height at which the stem divides; 0: never
param fork_stems;             # stems it divides into
param fork_angle;             # angle between the stem and each new stem
param thorns;                 # 1: a thorn beside each bud
param thorn_length;
param thorn_angle;            # angle of a thorn to its shoot
param thorn_area;             # leaf area of a thorn card 1 m long, m² (the default leaf card's)
param wind;                   # strength of a steady wind toward +X; 0 none
param wind_bend;              # extra downwind bending per unit of wind
param wind_kill;              # a tip heading upwind beyond this dies
param life;                   # age at which the plant dies; 0 never
param snag_fall;              # chance a year that a dead branch falls
param pipe_tip;               # radius of the twig behind one living bud
param pipe_organ;             # pipe radius per metre of leaf card
param pipe_rings;             # ring area laid down per m² of leaf a year
# Light extinction per unit of leaf area density. 0.5 suits leaves spread at
# random through each light voxel; leaves bunched on short shoots shade one
# another and let more light past, which a lower value stands for.
param extinction;
param light_cell;             # light voxel edge; smaller for shrubs
param space_density;          # attraction points per m³ of crown envelope
param space_reach;             # how far a bud senses free space
param space_kill;              # free space within this of the plant is taken
# Growth units and bud fate (revision 10).
param unit_nodes;             # nodes a year's shoot grows for each internode its vigour allows
param long_share;             # share of a year's shoot's nodes whose buds may grow long shoots; 1: every node
param short_share;            # share of its nodes, next below (or above) those, whose buds grow short shoots; the rest stay latent
param bud_base;               # 1: those nodes are the shoot's first (basitony); 0: its last (acrotony)
# Limbs that live by their own light (revision 10; the maples' since G1).
param shed_ratio;             # a limb older than shed_age is shed when qsum < shed_ratio * nseg; 0: only bare limbs
param shed_age;
param dormant_buds;           # 1: each node keeps a dormant bud that sprouts where light reaches
param dormant_years;          # years a dormant bud lives
param sprout_light;           # light at which a dormant bud sprouts
param dormant_angle;          # a dormant bud's angle from its shoot
param space_renew;            # 1: free space returns where the plant's parts are shed
param terminal_bloom;         # chance a year that a long shoot ends in flowers and forks
param twin_angle;             # angle of each twin shoot from the old axis
param apex_death;             # chance a year that a tip with no free space aborts
# The crown grows its own outline (revision 11).
param room_width;             # free space fills this many times the crown's radius
param room_height;            # and this many times its height
param crown_phototropism;     # how far the region's front turns toward its light (revision 14)
param path_half;              # wood from the base at which a shoot's nodes are half as long; 0: no limit
param limb_path;              # how many times a limb's wood counts toward path_half (1: as the stem's)
param leader_rate;            # how far each node of the stem turns back toward upright
param set_point;              # a limb's held angle from straight up
param incline_rate;           # how far each node of a limb turns toward set_point
param wood_density;           # kg/m³ of green wood
param wood_modulus;           # modulus of elasticity, MPa
param leaf_mass;              # kg per m² of leaf
param bend_set;               # share of each year's sag the wood keeps
param stem_bend;              # share of its sag the stem and a fork's stems take: reaction wood holds them up
param straighten;             # share of its kept bend the wood straightens each year
# Scaffold limbs and silhouettes (revision 16).
param limb_arch = 0;          # degrees a limb's held angle grows per metre of limb wood: limbs arch outward
param limb_set_max = 95;      # the most a limb's held angle grows to, from straight up
param flat_top = 0;           # share of the crown's height above which every shoot levels out (Troll's model); 0: none
param bole_clear = 0;         # 1: the stem sheds every branch below the crown's base
param crown_widest = 0.5;     # share of the region's depth at which it is widest
param crown_fullness = 2;     # the region's profile: 2 an ellipse, more toward a flat-ended cylinder
param bloom_stalk = 0;        # a solitary bloom's own stalk, metres; 0 for none

# An active bud. `split` is the height at which the stem forks: only the
# first stem carries one; every other bud carries 0.
module A(split) queries light, vigour, space, position;
module B queries light, vigour, space;    # a lateral bud or short shoot
module S queries vigour, position;                  # the base of a branch
module M(n, u, l);                        # n nodes still to form this year, of u in the growth unit, each l long
module Fk(n);                             # n stems still to start at a fork
module Q(n, k);                           # n leaf pairs still to unfold on a short shoot, its k-th pair first
module Bo(n);                             # n blooms still to place at a short shoot's tip
module Bs;                                # a bloom's own stalk, if it has one
module Wb(k);                             # k lateral buds still to place round a whorl's node
module Wk(k, s);                          # k short-shoot buds (s as K's) still to place round it
module Wl(k);                             # k leaves still to place round it
module K(s) queries light, vigour;        # a short-shoot bud (s 1): leafs out, never grows out; s 0: latent
module D queries light, space;            # a dormant bud

organ leaf leaf area leaf_area;
organ bloom flower area bloom_area;
organ thorn leaf as spine area thorn_area;
organ bloom_male flower area bloom_area;

tool light@1 { cell = light_cell, extinction = extinction, bud = 0.01 };
tool space@4 {
    base = crown_base * (1 - exp(-crown_rate * (t + 3))),
    height = room_height * crown_height * (1 - exp(-crown_rate * (t + 3))),
    radius = room_width * crown_radius * (1 - exp(-crown_rate * (t + 3))),
    ratio = room_width * crown_radius / max(room_height * crown_height - crown_base, 0.01),
    phototropism = crown_phototropism,
    widest = crown_widest,
    fullness = crown_fullness,
    density = space_density,
    influence = space_reach,
    kill = space_kill,
    angle = 80,
    renew = space_renew
};
tool vigour@1 {
    lambda = apical + (apical_young - apical) * max(0, 1 - t / apical_years),
    alpha = flux,
    saturation = light_half
};
tool bend@1 {
    density = wood_density,
    modulus = wood_modulus,
    leaf_mass = leaf_mass,
    set = bend_set,
    straighten = straighten,
    stem = stem_bend
};
# Each living bud's twig adds to the pipes below it, a growth unit's
# nodes sharing one bud's.
tool pipe@1 { exponent = 2.3, tip = pipe_tip / pow(unit_nodes, 1 / 2.3), organ = pipe_organ, rings = pipe_rings };

# The stem leans a little in a random direction; each tree forks at its own
# height. The droop bends each segment, so a growth unit's nodes share it.
axiom !(0.004) T(wind, -1, 0, (droop + wind_bend * wind) / unit_nodes) incline(0, leader_rate)
      /(uniform(0, 360)) &(uniform(0, lean))
      A(fork_height * uniform(0.7, 1.3));

# In a steady wind, a tip heading upwind dies.
rule A(split) : wind > 0 && hx < -wind_kill -> ;

# A plant past its life dies: its buds die.
rule A(split) : life > 0 && t >= life -> ;
rule B : life > 0 && t >= life -> ;

# Buds die in deep shade.
rule A(split) : light < shade_death -> ;
rule B : light < shade_death || age >= bud_years -> ;

# Where the stem reaches its fork height it divides into equal stems.
rule A(split) : split > 0 && py >= split && vigour >= 1 -> Fk(fork_stems);

# A long shoot in the light, old enough to flower, grows its year's nodes,
# ends them in a flower cluster and forks into twin shoots from the buds
# below it (terminal flowering: the cluster ends the year's growth, so a
# fork always stands on wood). Only lineages that set terminal_bloom
# (revision 10; the maples' since G1).
rule A(split) : terminal_bloom > 0 && blooms > 0 && t >= adult_age && split <= 0 && vigour >= 1
                && space > 0 && light >= spur_light && (life <= 0 || t < life)
                && rand() < terminal_bloom ->
    steer(sx, sy, sz, steer_weight)
    M(min(floor(vigour), max_shoot) * unit_nodes,
      min(floor(vigour), max_shoot) * unit_nodes,
      internode / unit_nodes / (path_half > 0 ? 1 + pow((path + (limb_path - 1) * limb) / path_half, 2) : 1))
    Bo(blooms) /(divergence) [ &(twin_angle) S A(0) ] [ /(180) &(twin_angle) S A(0) ];

# Near the crown's top, every shoot levels out (flat_top, revision 16),
# the stem too: umbrella crowns whose axes all turn to spread.
rule A(split) : flat_top > 0 && split <= 0 && py > flat_top * crown_height * (1 - exp(-crown_rate * (t + 3)))
                && vigour >= 1 && space > 0 ->
    incline(limb_set_max, incline_rate)
    steer(sx, sy, sz, steer_weight)
    M(min(floor(vigour), max_shoot) * unit_nodes,
      min(floor(vigour), max_shoot) * unit_nodes,
      internode / unit_nodes / (path_half > 0 ? 1 + pow((path + (limb_path - 1) * limb) / path_half, 2) : 1)) A(split);

# On a limb, a shoot holds a set point that grows with the limb's wood
# (limb_arch, revision 16), so limbs rise from the stem and arch outward.
rule A(split) : limb_arch > 0 && limb > 0 && vigour >= 1 && space > 0 ->
    incline(min(set_point + limb_arch * limb, limb_set_max), incline_rate)
    steer(sx, sy, sz, steer_weight)
    M(min(floor(vigour), max_shoot) * unit_nodes,
      min(floor(vigour), max_shoot) * unit_nodes,
      internode / unit_nodes / (path_half > 0 ? 1 + pow((path + (limb_path - 1) * limb) / path_half, 2) : 1)) A(split);

# An active bud with vigour and free space ahead grows a shoot; far out
# along the wood its nodes are shorter (path_half, revision 11).
rule A(split) : vigour >= 1 && space > 0 ->
    steer(sx, sy, sz, steer_weight)
    M(min(floor(vigour), max_shoot) * unit_nodes,
      min(floor(vigour), max_shoot) * unit_nodes,
      internode / unit_nodes / (path_half > 0 ? 1 + pow((path + (limb_path - 1) * limb) / path_half, 2) : 1)) A(split);

# A lateral bud breaks into a long shoot when it has the vigour and free
# space; otherwise, in enough light, it leafs out as a short shoot.
rule B : vigour >= bud_break && space > 0 -> A(0);
rule B : light >= spur_light && blooms > 0 && t >= adult_age && bloom_stalk <= 0 -> Q(spur_pairs, age * spur_pairs) Bo(blooms) B;
rule B : light >= spur_light && (blooms <= 0 || t < adult_age || bloom_stalk <= 0) -> Q(spur_pairs, age * spur_pairs) B;

# One internode, turned a little at random, with a pair of buds and a pair
# of leaves; the next pair is turned by divergence (a quarter turn:
# decussate). Alternate species grow theirs by the last rules of the
# program.
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node >= 2 && thorns <= 0 && dormant_buds <= 0 && leaves_per_node < 3
                    && (long_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < long_share * u : n <= long_share * u)) ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ] [ /(180) &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ]
    [ &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ] [ /(180) &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n <= 0 -> ;

# The new stems of a fork, spread evenly round the old one; each is a branch
# of its own, so a stem that dies is shed.
decompose Fk(n) : n > 0 ->
    [ /(360 * n / fork_stems + uniform(-25, 25)) &(fork_angle + uniform(-8, 8)) S A(0) ]
    Fk(n - 1);
decompose Fk(n) -> ;

# A short shoot's leaves crowded at its tip: two single ones, or a pair,
# for each of spur_pairs, each turned by divergence from the one before,
# year after year: the k-th pair since the shoot began stands k
# divergences round (two single leaves a pair).
decompose Q(n, k) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node < 2 ->
    leaf(spur_leaf, divergence * 2 * k, leaf_angle, 1)
    leaf(spur_leaf, divergence * (2 * k + 1), leaf_angle, 1)
    Q(n - 1, k + 1);
decompose Q(n, k) : n > 0 ->
    leaf(spur_leaf, divergence * k, leaf_angle, 1) leaf(spur_leaf, divergence * k + 180, leaf_angle, 1)
    Q(n - 1, k + 1);
decompose Q(n, k) -> ;


# Leaves fall after leaf_years; blooms, a male plant's too, last one year.
rule leaf(s) : age + dt >= leaf_years -> ;
rule bloom(s) : age + dt >= 1 -> ;
rule bloom_male(s) : age + dt >= 1 -> ;

# A clear bole (revision 16): a branch whose base stands below the
# crown's base, as it rises with the tree, is shed; never at or above
# where the stem forks, so a fork's stems stand.
rule S : bole_clear > 0 && age > 2
         && py < min(crown_base * (1 - exp(-crown_rate * (t + 3))), fork_height > 0 ? 0.7 * fork_height : crown_base) -> %;

# A branch with no living bud is shed; on a dead plant, one by one (the
# last rules).
rule S : age > 1 && ntip == 0 && (life <= 0 || t < life) -> %;

# Rules with random draws that later revisions add go last, so the draws of
# the rules above keep their sites and species that do not use them grow as
# before.

# An alternate species' internode: one bud and one leaf, the next turned
# by divergence (137.5° on the spiral).
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node < 2 && thorns <= 0 && dormant_buds <= 0
                    && (long_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < long_share * u : n <= long_share * u)) ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ] [ &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);

# Blooms spread round a short shoot's tip: a male plant's are male, set
# with no random draws (they vary by their place), so every rule's draws
# keep their sites.
decompose Bo(n) : n > 0 && dioecious >= 0.5 && sex < 0.5 && bloom_stalk <= 0 ->
    [ /(n * 137.5 + 40 * frac(n * 0.618) - 20) &(bloom_angle * (0.8 + 0.4 * frac(n * 0.382)))
      bloom_male(bloom_size * (0.85 + 0.3 * frac(n * 0.754))) ]
    Bo(n - 1);
decompose Bo(n) : n > 0 && bloom_stalk <= 0 ->
    [ /(n * 137.5 + uniform(-20, 20)) &(bloom_angle * uniform(0.8, 1.2))
      bloom(bloom_size * uniform(0.85, 1.15)) ]
    Bo(n - 1);
decompose Bo(n) : bloom_stalk <= 0 -> ;

# Revision 4 (plant forms F5). A thorny species' internodes: as above, with
# a thorn beside each bud.
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node >= 2 && (thorns > 0 || (dormant_buds <= 0 && leaves_per_node < 3))
                    && (long_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < long_share * u : n <= long_share * u)) ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ] [ /(180) &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ]
    [ &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ] [ /(180) &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ]
    [ /(90) &(thorn_angle) thorn(thorn_length * uniform(0.8, 1.2)) ]
    [ /(270) &(thorn_angle) thorn(thorn_length * uniform(0.8, 1.2)) ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node < 2 && (thorns > 0 || dormant_buds <= 0)
                    && (long_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < long_share * u : n <= long_share * u)) ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ] [ &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ]
    [ /(70) &(thorn_angle) thorn(thorn_length * uniform(0.8, 1.2)) ]
    [ /(-70) &(thorn_angle) thorn(thorn_length * uniform(0.8, 1.2)) ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);

# A dead plant's branches fall one by one.
rule S : age > 1 && ntip == 0 && rand() < snag_fall -> %;

# Revision 10 (crown form, step A). These rules go last so the draws of
# the rules above keep their sites.

# A shoot tip with no free space before it aborts with the chance
# apex_death a year. Without it a tip in good light that cannot grow lives
# for ever and keeps its leafless limb, and shedding never takes it.
rule A(split) : apex_death > 0 && space <= 0 && t > 10 && rand() < apex_death -> ;

# A tip with no free space left that lives on leafs out as a short shoot
# does, in enough light (revision 11), so the crown's edge keeps its leaves.
rule A(split) : light >= spur_light && space <= 0 -> Q(spur_pairs, age * spur_pairs) A(split);

# A limb that no longer pays its way is shed, as in Pałubicki et al.
# (2009): the light its tips collect, qsum, over the internodes it carries,
# nseg, falls below shed_ratio. Only limbs older than shed_age, so young
# shoots have time to leaf out.
rule S : shed_ratio > 0 && age > shed_age && qsum < shed_ratio * nseg -> %;

# A short-shoot bud: like a lateral bud that never has the vigour to grow
# out. It leafs out each year in the light, flowers once the plant is
# adult, and dies in deep shade or old. A latent bud (s 0), on the nodes
# past the short shoots, never grows.
rule K(s) : s <= 0 -> ;
rule K(s) : life > 0 && t >= life -> ;
rule K(s) : light < shade_death || age >= bud_years -> ;
rule K(s) : light >= spur_light && blooms > 0 && t >= adult_age && bloom_stalk <= 0 -> Q(spur_pairs, age * spur_pairs) Bo(blooms) K(s);
rule K(s) : light >= spur_light && (blooms <= 0 || t < adult_age || bloom_stalk <= 0) -> Q(spur_pairs, age * spur_pairs) K(s);

# Dormant buds and reiteration: most of an old crown's leafy shoots come
# from buds that wait on its limbs, not from the branching of its tips
# (Ishii and Ford 2001), and sprouts fill a crown's gaps and inside. With
# dormant_buds, each node keeps one, a quarter turn round from its
# laterals; it sprouts into a long shoot when light reaches it with free
# space before it, and dies after dormant_years.
rule D : age >= dormant_years -> ;
rule D : light >= sprout_light && space > 0 -> incline(set_point, incline_rate) S A(0);

# A growth unit's node whose buds may not grow long shoots: short-shoot
# buds (K) in place of lateral buds (B), the short_share of the unit's
# nodes next to the long ones, and latent buds on the rest. And, with
# dormant_buds, every node keeps a dormant bud D.
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node >= 2 && thorns <= 0 && dormant_buds <= 0 && leaves_per_node < 3 ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) S K((short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) ] [ /(180) &(branch_angle) S K((short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) ]
    [ &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ] [ /(180) &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node < 2 && thorns <= 0 && dormant_buds <= 0 ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) S K((short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) ] [ &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node >= 2 && thorns <= 0 && (dormant_buds > 0 || leaves_per_node < 3)
                    && (long_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < long_share * u : n <= long_share * u)) ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ] [ /(180) &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ]
    leaf(leaf_size, 0, leaf_angle, 1) leaf(leaf_size, 180, leaf_angle, 1)
    [ /(90) &(dormant_angle) D ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node >= 2 && thorns <= 0 && (dormant_buds > 0 || leaves_per_node < 3) ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) S K((short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) ] [ /(180) &(branch_angle) S K((short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) ]
    leaf(leaf_size, 0, leaf_angle, 1) leaf(leaf_size, 180, leaf_angle, 1)
    [ /(90) &(dormant_angle) D ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node < 2 && thorns <= 0
                    && (long_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < long_share * u : n <= long_share * u)) ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ] leaf(leaf_size, 0, leaf_angle, 1)
    [ /(180) &(dormant_angle) D ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node < 2 && thorns <= 0 ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) S K((short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) ] leaf(leaf_size, 0, leaf_angle, 1)
    [ /(180) &(dormant_angle) D ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node >= 2 && (thorns > 0 || dormant_buds > 0 || leaves_per_node < 3) ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) S K((short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) ] [ /(180) &(branch_angle) S K((short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) ]
    [ &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ] [ /(180) &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ]
    [ /(90) &(thorn_angle) thorn(thorn_length * uniform(0.8, 1.2)) ]
    [ /(270) &(thorn_angle) thorn(thorn_length * uniform(0.8, 1.2)) ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node < 2 ->
    ^(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +(gauss() * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    [ &(branch_angle) S K((short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) ] [ &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ]
    [ /(70) &(thorn_angle) thorn(thorn_length * uniform(0.8, 1.2)) ]
    [ /(-70) &(thorn_angle) thorn(thorn_length * uniform(0.8, 1.2)) ]
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);

# Blooms on stalks of their own (revision 17): as the blooms above, each
# on a thin stalk bloom_stalk long, hanging from its short shoot as its
# angle leans it. A plant without stalks places its blooms by the rules
# above, as it did. These spread their blooms by the bloom's place in the
# shoot, as the male blooms do, with no draw of their own: a draw here
# would renumber the draws of every program that extends this one. The
# stalk is a branch of its own (S), with no bud, so it is shed with the
# bloom's year rather than left standing.
decompose Bo(n) : n > 0 && dioecious >= 0.5 && sex < 0.5 ->
    [ /(n * 137.5 + 40 * frac(n * 0.618) - 20) &(bloom_angle * (0.8 + 0.4 * frac(n * 0.382)))
      S Bs bloom_male(bloom_size * (0.85 + 0.3 * frac(n * 0.754))) ]
    Bo(n - 1);
decompose Bo(n) : n > 0 ->
    [ /(n * 137.5 + 40 * frac(n * 0.618) - 20) &(bloom_angle * (0.8 + 0.4 * frac(n * 0.382)))
      S Bs bloom(bloom_size * (0.85 + 0.3 * frac(n * 0.754))) ]
    Bo(n - 1);
decompose Bo(n) -> ;
decompose Bs -> !(bloom_size * 0.03) F(bloom_stalk);

# A bud or short shoot whose blooms stand on stalks of their own grows a
# sliver of wood the year it flowers, at its own depth, for the stalks to
# stand on: a stalk drawn straight from the bud would be wood two orders
# above the shoot that bears it, with none between.
rule K(s) : light >= spur_light && blooms > 0 && t >= adult_age ->
    !(bloom_size * 0.04) F(0.002) Q(spur_pairs, age * spur_pairs) Bo(blooms) K(s);
rule B : light >= spur_light && blooms > 0 && t >= adult_age ->
    !(bloom_size * 0.04) F(0.002) Q(spur_pairs, age * spur_pairs) Bo(blooms) B;

# Leaves in whorls of three or more (revision 18), a fuchsia's: the
# whorl's buds and leaves spread evenly round the node, the next whorl
# turned by divergence. Only an unarmed species with no dormant buds; the
# rules above draw the rest in pairs. Each internode leans by its place in
# the unit, with no draw of its own, so no program's draws renumber.
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node >= 3
                    && (long_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < long_share * u : n <= long_share * u)) ->
    ^((frac(n * 0.618 + u * 0.382) - 0.5) * 2 * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +((frac(n * 0.754 + u * 0.291) - 0.5) * 2 * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    Wb(leaves_per_node) Wl(leaves_per_node)
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose M(n, u, l) : n > 0 && leaves_per_node >= 3 ->
    ^((frac(n * 0.618 + u * 0.382) - 0.5) * 2 * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) +((frac(n * 0.754 + u * 0.291) - 0.5) * 2 * wiggle / sqrt(unit_nodes)) F(l)
    Wk(leaves_per_node, (short_share >= 1 || (bud_base > 0 ? u - n < (long_share + short_share) * u : n <= (long_share + short_share) * u) ? 1 : 0)) Wl(leaves_per_node)
    /(divergence) M(n - 1, u, l);
decompose Wb(k) : k > 0 ->
    [ /(360 * k / leaves_per_node) &(branch_angle) incline(set_point, incline_rate) S B ] Wb(k - 1);
decompose Wb(k) -> ;
decompose Wk(k, s) : k > 0 -> [ /(360 * k / leaves_per_node) &(branch_angle) S K(s) ] Wk(k - 1, s);
decompose Wk(k, s) -> ;
decompose Wl(k) : k > 0 -> [ /(360 * k / leaves_per_node) &(leaf_angle) $ leaf(leaf_size) ] Wl(k - 1);
decompose Wl(k) -> ;

